TITLE:: RLFit
summary:: A list of chords read as passages, each in one context, at the least total cost
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLScore, Classes/RLRegions, Classes/RLScale, Classes/RLChordContext, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
Any two triads are joined by an arrow in every group context, so "is there an arrow" tells nothing: a reading is worth what it saves. Each chord, given the one before, has a cost in each candidate context, each change of context a cost, and the fit is the cheapest way through the piece (a dynamic programme over the chords).

The contexts are the regions round a tonic (link::Classes/RLRegions::) and the triads under P, L, R. In a region a chord is one of nine kinds: the degree of its root, 0 to 6, when its tones are tones of the scale; 7, an artificial dominant (a foreign chord with a major third whose root goes a fourth up to a chord of the region, or a diminished one a semitone under its goal; it may be held up to three chords); 8, another foreign chord. A chord reached from another context is priced as a step of the new one, the chord before read there too: a pivot.

Two models of the costs:
definitionlist::
## hand-set (nil) || link::#*defaultCosts::: a step priced by Schoenberg's kind of root progression (link::Classes/RLScale#-progression::), a change of region by its class times a number. A fallback, and what the tests use.
## counted || link::#*readModel::: how often each kind of chord follows each in a corpus of analysed scores, how often and how far the key changes, as bits. The cost of a reading is then the length of its description, and a passage is in a key when saying so is shorter than not. Count the model on other pieces than the one read.
::

A chord written again (the root and the tones of the chord before: another inversion, a repetition) is that chord going on, when the model has code::\again::: it costs that (0 in the counted models) in every context, and is not one of the three chords an artificial dominant may be held. How often a held chord is written again is the writer's habit, not the music's. With every label counted as a step, a chord that follows itself has a price by its degree, and a dominant follows itself more cheaply than a tonic (it is the chord that gains a seventh: V, V7): a piece that sits on its tonic chord, written again at each inversion, is then cheaper read as a dominant, a fifth below its key. The hand-set model prices every label unless asked: code::RLFit(chords, regions, (again: 0))::.

code::
~c = RLScale.major(RLEDO(12));
~chords = RLFit.events([0, 3, 6, 2, 5, 1, 3, 4, 0].collect { |d| ~c.triads.chord(d) }, ~c);
~fit = RLFit(~chords, RLRegions(RLEDO(12)));
~fit.segments.first[\numerals];        // I IV viio iii vi ii IV V I
~fit.segments.first[\patterns];        // the roots a fourth up, five times
~fit.surprises;                        // after ii the ring asks for V: IV came
~fit.report.postln;

~score = RLScore.read(path);
~fit = RLFit(~score.chords, ~score.regions, RLFit.readModel(modelPath));
~fit.agreement;                        // with the keys the analysts wrote
~fit.report(~score).postln;
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: chords
Events with code::\pcs:: and code::\root:: (pitch classes of the regions' system), and what else they have: code::\onset::, code::\dur::, code::\mn::, code::\key:: (the region an analyst wrote).
argument:: regions
An link::Classes/RLRegions::.
argument:: model
nil, entries of the hand-set table to change, or a counted model.
argument:: span
The regions tried: those within so many fifths of the tonic.

METHOD:: choosing
A fit of chords that come with the other chords their spans could be (code::\alternatives::, each with code::\extra::: link::Classes/RLChordFit#-withAlternatives::). Where the notes price two chords alike, the passage chooses: a six-four before its dominant, a diminished chord and the seventh chord it is the top of. One programme over the chords, the contexts and the alternatives; the choice is kept only when the whole is cheaper (the fit's cost and what the notes cost more). The fit returned is that of the chosen chords, with link::#-chosen:: and link::#-extra::.

code::
~chords = RLChordFit(~score);
~fit = RLFit.choosing(~chords.withAlternatives, ~score.regions);
~fit.chosen.count { |x| x > 0 };     // how many chords the passage changed
~fit.extra;                          // what that costs in the notes
::

METHOD:: events
Chords for a fit from link::Classes/RLChord::s, of a space of the system or of a scale's space (given the scale).

METHOD:: periods
The runs of a word that repeat a shorter word: at least two units and three steps.

METHOD:: defaultCosts
METHOD:: handModel
METHOD:: readModel

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: segments
The passages, each an Event: code::\first::, code::\last:: (chords), code::\from::, code::\to:: (time), code::\kind:: (code::\region:: or code::\triads::), code::\region::, code::\name::, code::\relation:: (its class from the tonic), code::\scale::, code::\numerals::, code::\word:: (the steps between roots, or P, L, R words), code::\progressions::, code::\patterns::, code::\cost::. The passages' costs add up to the fit's.

METHOD:: path
The context of each chord, as an index into link::#-states::.
METHOD:: states
METHOD:: cost
METHOD:: costs
The model used.

METHOD:: chosen
After link::#*choosing::: per chord, 0 or the number of the alternative taken.
METHOD:: extra
After link::#*choosing::: what the choices cost more in the notes.

METHOD:: surprises
What stands out: a foreign chord that leads nowhere, a pattern of three units or more that stops before its passage does (with what one more step would have been, and the steps between that and what came), a change to a region of class 3 or beyond.

METHOD:: agreement
How long the fit's regions are the keys the chords carry: code::[quarter notes agreed, labelled]::.
METHOD:: agreementWith
The same against chords an analyst wrote on their own time line (each with code::\onset::, code::\dur::, code::\key::), for a fit of other chords than theirs (link::Classes/RLChordFit::'s).

METHOD:: differences
Where they are not.

METHOD:: coverage
Per passage, how much of a score's notes its chords hold, and its scale, with and without its substitutes.

METHOD:: title
METHOD:: regionTitle
METHOD:: report
The reading as text; with a score, the coverage too.

METHOD:: data
The reading as plain data (numbers, Strings, Arrays and Events of those), for a file or a page: the contexts it
could choose from (each region's name, class, tonic and scale; Schoenberg's chart), each chord as read (its
context, passage, numeral, kind, the step into it, what it cost and what the change into its context cost), the
passages with their patterns, the surprises, where the reading differs from the keys the chords carry. With a
score, the coverage too. HomewareSC's code::Math/Category_Theory/fit/:: writes it as JSON and shows it as a page.
